 Keep the existing output reservation and token accounting. The default safety buffer is the smaller of 13K and 10% of the effective input window, so a small but positive window does not compact after a few tokens. Explicit buffer values (including zero) retain precedence. The 200K/1M defaults, disabled state and failure circuit breaker retain their behavior. A zero effective input budget is still a separate unresolved request-budget boundary; no artificial positive threshold is created. `packages/core/test/compact-policy.test.ts` covers the bounded change.
 
 The context popup follows the upstream capacity → visible composition → compact allowance order. The owner rejected the added Tabs and ledger-first hierarchy. Request counters and cache rate stay accessible in a secondary disclosure; character-estimated composition is visible and marked as an estimate. A valid restored context sample may show its last recorded ratio with an explicit Last label. Quota remains reachable before the first message without an invented zero count. No account mutation occurs on this display path.
+
+## Usage costs and subscription payments (OV-047)
+
+The owner approved extending/migrating the existing usage ledger. Each model_usage row owns a
+compact accounting snapshot: reported counters, provider/account identity when actually resolved,
+requested/served speed, sourced price version and API-equivalent/native-credit estimates. Old rows
+migrate reported counters only; current settings never backfill historical account or speed. Keep
+small usage facts across months; explicit cleanup remains separate from automatic raw-I/O retention.
+The shared pure calculator accepts exact billing provider/model, request time, inclusive input/cache
+counters, output, speed and authentication kind. Unknown prices/tiers/counters remain unknown.
+
+App Settings owns user-entered payment records keyed by ID, with provider/account, [start,end),
+currency and paid amount. Its existing serialized write queue merges individual payment keys.
+The existing usage query accepts an explicit bounded period and returns account/model/mode groups;
+no second database, credential owner or billing service. Allocation uses native credit weights when
+all account-period rows support them, otherwise complete official API-value weights. Missing rows,
+no usage and unpriced models leave the payment unallocated. Only observed Fleet usage is covered;
+ongoing billing periods are provisional and mixed currencies are never summed. Display per-model
+cache ratio as summed reported cache reads divided by the corresponding reported total input.
+Token popup retains original context/allowance shape; request/cost analytics lives in Usage only.
